cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository in your research, tools, or publications, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Opencir Skills"
abstract: >
  A structured collection of 653 cybersecurity skills for AI agents, scoped to
  security research, defense, and education: digital forensics, threat
  intelligence, incident response, detection engineering, cloud security,
  OT/SCADA security, AI security, and more. Each skill follows a standardized
  format with YAML frontmatter metadata, step-by-step procedures, tool
  commands, expected outputs, and framework mappings. Compatible with Claude
  Code, GitHub Copilot, Cursor, Windsurf, Gemini CLI, and other AI agent
  platforms. Forked from Anthropic-Cybersecurity-Skills by Mahipal Jangra
  (mukul975), with offensive and dual-use penetration-testing/red-team
  content removed.
